ding Rounds Went Well but LLD Did Not",author:"Anonymous",postedAt:"2 months ago",excerpt:"The Swiggy interview process was spread across 4–5 weeks and had a mix of DSA, Golang basics, a Bar Raiser discussion, and Low-Level Design.",company:"Swiggy",upvotes:1,comments:0,views:48},{id:"google-l4",title:"Google L4 Interview: Six Rounds, One Valuable Lesson",author:"Aarav Mehta",postedAt:"3 weeks ago",excerpt:"A detailed breakdown of phone screening, graph problems, system design, and the behavioural round that changed how I prepare.",company:"Google",upvotes:28,comments:14,views:742},{id:"amazon-sde2",title:"Amazon SDE-2 Interview Experience — From OA to Bar Raiser",author:"Neha Kapoor",postedAt:"1 month ago",excerpt:"Each round tested a different signal: problem solving, ownership, design depth, and how clearly I communicated trade-offs.",company:"Amazon",upvotes:19,comments:7,views:516},{id:"atlassian-graduate",title:"How I Prepared for Atlassian Graduate Software Engineer",author:"Rohan Shah",postedAt:"8 days ago",excerpt:"The process included a coding assessment, values interview, data structures round, and a practical machine-coding exercise.",company:"Atlassian",upvotes:13,comments:5,views:306},{id:"microsoft-campus",title:"Microsoft Campus Placement: The Questions I Was Actually Asked",author:"Priya Singh",postedAt:"12 days ago",excerpt:"Sharing the exact topics from my technical rounds, how the interviewers gave hints, and what helped me recover after getting stuck.",company:"Microsoft",upvotes:31,comments:18,views:893},{id:"uber-backend",title:"Uber Backend Engineer Interview — DSA, Design and Debugging",author:"Kabir Joshi",postedAt:"5 days ago",excerpt:"My loop combined algorithmic reasoning with a real-world debugging scenario and a scalable ride-matching design discussion.",company:"Uber",upvotes:16,comments:6,views:427},{id:"flipkart-machine-coding",title:"Flipkart SDE Interview: Machine Coding Round Walkthrough",author:"Meera Nair",postedAt:"2 weeks ago",excerpt:"I built a small inventory service under time pressure. Here is how I scoped the requirements and kept the design extensible.",company:"Flipkart",upvotes:22,comments:11,views:604},{id:"meta-product-engineer",title:"Meta Product Engineer Loop: Coding, Product Sense and Team Match",author:"Ishaan Verma",postedAt:"4 days ago",excerpt:"Two fast-paced coding rounds were followed by product architecture and behavioural conversations focused on impact and collaboration.",company:"Meta",upvotes:37,comments:16,views:1042,topComment:{author:"Ananya Rao",postedAt:"2d ago",message:"The team-match explanation cleared up a lot of confusion."}},{id:"goldman-analyst",title:"Goldman Sachs Analyst Interview: What Happened After the HackerRank",author:"Sanya Gupta",postedAt:"3 weeks ago",excerpt:"The technical discussion moved from arrays and SQL to resume projects, operating systems, and a short design problem.",company:"Goldman Sachs",upvotes:18,comments:8,views:469},{id:"razorpay-platform",title:"Razorpay Platform Engineer — My Complete Backend Interview Journey",author:"Dev Malhotra",postedAt:"6 days ago",excerpt:"I was asked to reason about idempotent payments, database consistency, service boundaries, and failure recovery before writing code.",company:"Razorpay",upvotes:26,comments:12,views:681},{id:"nvidia-systems",title:"NVIDIA Systems Software Interview: C++, Concurrency and Memory",author:"Aditya Kulkarni",postedAt:"9 days ago",excerpt:"A round-by-round account covering modern C++, thread synchronization, cache behaviour, debugging, and one medium graph problem.",company:"NVIDIA",upvotes:24,comments:10,views:738,topComment:{author:"Rahul Jain",postedAt:"5d ago",message:"Excellent list of C++ topics to revise before the onsite."}},{id:"salesforce-mts",title:"Salesforce MTS Interview Experience — Preparation to Offer",author:"Tanvi Bhat",postedAt:"2 days ago",excerpt:"The interviewers cared as much about clean APIs and testing strategy as the final algorithm. Here are the questions and my approach.",company:"Salesforce",upvotes:15,comments:4,views:318},{id:"phonepe-android",title:"PhonePe Android Engineer: Architecture and Live Coding Rounds",author:"Arjun Menon",postedAt:"1 week ago",excerpt:"The loop covered Kotlin coroutines, app architecture, performance profiling, and a live coding task with changing requirements.",company:"PhonePe",upvotes:21,comments:9,views:572},{id:"adobe-member-technical",title:"Adobe Member of Technical Staff — Off-Campus Interview Experience",author:"Nandini Bose",postedAt:"11 days ago",excerpt:"After the online assessment, I faced two DSA rounds, object-oriented design, and a hiring-manager conversation about past projects.",company:"Adobe",upvotes:17,comments:7,views:445},{id:"jpmorgan-fullstack",title:"JPMorgan Full-Stack Developer Interview: Java, React and Design",author:"Vikram Desai",postedAt:"5 days ago",excerpt:"A practical interview loop spanning Java collections, React rendering, REST API design, database indexing, and production debugging.",company:"JPMorgan",upvotes:12,comments:5,views:354,topComment:{author:"Simran Kaur",postedAt:"3d ago",message:"This is the most balanced full-stack round summary I found."}}],"LANDING_FEATURES_V2_PLANLY",0,[{id:"planly",label:"Planly",title:"Planly",subFeatures:[{id:"about-you",label:"About you",description:"Share your role, experience, and timeline so Planly can shape a plan that fits you."},{id:"understanding-your-goals",label:"Understanding your goals",description:"Planly reads your answers and turns them into a clear preparation direction before building your roadmap."},{id:"personalised-roadmap",label:"Personalised weekly sprints",description:"Turn one big goal into focused weekly sprints shaped around your level, deadline, and available time."},{id:"daily-tasks",label:"Solve & Practice",description:"Open Planly and know exactly what today needs—learn, revise, or practise."},{id:"learning-timer",label:"Track your time",description:"Replace guessw